  <!--========================= WA_ShojiBase =============================-->
  <ThingDef ParentName="WA_DoorBase" Name="WA_ShojiBase" Abstract="True">
    <label>Shoji</label>
    <description>Shoji paper is made by stretching thin paper in a grid-like framework. You can hide faint in the light.
It is very light, so you can open and close quickly, but durability is low.
It is said that the same form as the modern screed shoji appeared was around the time of the Kiyomori before the Kamakura period.
Because it is a structure that is extremely easy to break, it is a daily routine to open a hole in a shoji in a house with pets and children.</description>
    <statBases>
    </statBases>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Door/WA-Shoji01_Normal</texPath>
    </graphicData>
